content.text:
Now Hud.tsx add useEffect for focus. It already imports useEffect, useState. Add in FullHud:
```
useEffect(() => {
  if (!navigation) return;
  const timer = window.setTimeout(() => navigation.focusIndex(0), 180);
  return () => window.clearTimeout(timer);
}, [incident.id, navigation?.focusIndex]);
```
But eslint deps? No lint. `navigation` object changes; use destructured `focusIndex`:
```
const focusIndex = navigation?.focusIndex;
useEffect(() => { if (!focusIndex) return; const timer = ...; return ...; }, [focusIndex, incident.id]);
```
`focusIndex` stable if count same. But when count changes (same scenario always 3), stable. Good.
Potential issue: focus after 180ms, but the HUD entrance animation is 620ms; focus ring appears early. Fine. Could 300ms. Use 220ms.
Need to avoid focusing when user is interacting with sound/back? On new incident, focus action 1 is expected. If user clicks sound toggle during entrance, focus could steal after 220ms. Minor. Use 320ms and only if activeElement is body or within HUD? Check:
```
if (document.activeElement === document.body || document.activeElement?.closest(".hud")) focusIndex(0)
```
But when HUD opens, activeElement is body; good. If user clicked sound, activeElement is sound button (outside HUD), skip. If user clicked Back, skip. Good.
```
const active = document.activeElement;
if (active && active !== document.body && !(active instanceof HTMLElement && active.closest(".hud--full"))) return;
```
Then focus. Implement.

Also add `aria-label` to action buttons? They have visible text. Fine.

